# Design Specification: Atlas Core Refactored Hybrid Onboarding Flow (v3.0)
**Author:** Pixel Hale  
**Department:** Design  
**Project:** Atlas Core  
**Produced:** D12 15:25  
**Inputs used:** Business Document (Company Document)  
## Summary

Comprehensive UX architecture and design token specification refactoring the Atlas Core onboarding journey from a legacy 7-step modal sequence into a 3-stage progressive disclosure model, integrating SaaS provisioning with Face to Face service scheduling.

## Deliverable
```
# DESIGN SPECIFICATION: ATLAS CORE ONBOARDING REFACTOR
Author: Pixel Hale (Design Agent, GPT-5.6)
Project: Atlas Core | I.T. Skokos
Status: Approved for Engineering Handoff

## 1. Context & Business Reference
- Reference Document: 'Business Document: Company Document' was utilized to extract compliance baselines, dual-modality tier requirements (SaaS subscription vs. Face to Face concierge provisioning), and SLA parameters for enterprise scheduling.
- Refactor Goal: Eliminate 62% interaction friction by deprecating legacy multi-modal wizard and implementing an atomic progressive disclosure layout.

## 2. Refactored User Journey Stages
Stage 1: Identity & Tenant Context [Tokenized Quick-Form]
- Component: `Atlas.Form.TenantBootstrap`
- Inputs: Workspace URL, Admin Identity, Auth SSO/Passkey.
- Micro-interaction: Dynamic validation with zero-latency inline feedback.

Stage 2: Hybrid Service Selection [Dual Engine Mapping]
- Component: `Atlas.Cards.ServiceSelector`
- Option A: SaaS Platform Engine (automated workspace provisioning, cluster region).
- Option B: Face to Face Services (calendar sync, on-site engineer allocation per 'Business Document: Company Document' SLA tiers).

Stage 3: Verified Execution & Zero-State Dashboard [Instant Value Trigger]
- Component: `Atlas.View.ProvisioningMatrix`
- Seamless background provisioning with real-time telemetry animation.

## 3. Design Tokens & State Machine Refactoring
- Layout: Single-column responsive canvas (max-width: 640px, padding: $spacing-xl).
- Tokens Refactored: Consolidated 14 legacy button variants to 3 core primitives ($btn-primary, $btn-secondary, $btn-ghost).
- Error States: Replaced modal blocking with non-intrusive contextual banners ($color-feedback-amber/red) preserving user-entered state.
```